  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0a29b0691cda5cc409134a7d16c56213, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'To the owner,


    Forgive the sudden letter. I read about your shop
    online, a place where one cook serves six countries. In Japan we say a person
    should master one thing. You seem to be trying six. I respect that.


    I am
    Kenji Morita. I fry tonkatsu in a small shop near a train station in Osaka. Students,
    salarymen, old men alone. They all sit at the same counter.


    Pound the pork,
    bread it carefully, fry it twice if you must. Shred the cabbage so fine it looks
    like snow.


    Simple food, done properly, is never simple.'
